Description: read node-monitor messages through the virtual ref fields
 V\OS node-monitor messages carry no node/directory/device integer fields
 (device is uint64 when present at all); upstream's FindInt64("node"),
 FindInt32("device"), FindInt64("from/to directory") reads compile but never
 match, so the add-ons watcher, the list renames and the remove handler
 silently do nothing. Read FindNodeRef("virtual:node") and
 FindRef("virtual:directory"/"virtual:from directory"/"virtual:to
 directory") instead and stop rebuilding refs from integers. The
 B_DEVICE_MOUNTED/UNMOUNTED device values are uint64 now (FindUInt64), and
 the app's own device messages follow V\OS's 64-bit dev_t instead of int32.
 entry_ref/node_ref fields are accessors on V\OS, so the surviving field
 reads become device()/node() calls (real-identity values, == compares real
 identity); no ref field is assigned anywhere anymore.
Author: Numerio <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Forwarded: no
Origin: https://github.com/HaikuArchives/Hare

